            <fr:title text="Sequential Ambiguity Helper">Sequential Ambiguity Helper</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Daily</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
  Max suggested that an effective way to represent <fr:link href="/sss-0017/" title="Sequential Unambiguity" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-0017/" display-uri="sss-0017" type="local">sequential unamiguity</fr:link> in Dependent Lambek Calculus to alleviate my issues proving <fr:link href="/sss-000V/" title="FollowLast Soundness" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-000V/" display-uri="sss-000V" type="local">followlast soundness</fr:link>.
</html:p>
            <html:p>
  An attempt would be that the following map has an inverse
  <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[g \otimes  {\mathopen {}\left ({\mathopen {}\left (h \otimes  k\right )\mathclose {}} \And  {\mathopen {}\left (h \otimes  l\right )\mathclose {}}\right )\mathclose {}} \vdash  {\mathopen {}\left (g \otimes  h \otimes  k\right )\mathclose {}} \And  (g \otimes  h \otimes  l)]]></fr:tex></html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
